1
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:27,400
Thank you very much.

2
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:29,480
I got some good practice in thanks to you.

3
00:00:29,480 --> 00:00:30,400
N-No problem.

4
00:00:31,110 --> 00:00:32,200
No way!

5
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:34,030
Is he really a middle schooler?

6
00:00:34,030 --> 00:00:36,280
Not even a college player can 
cleanly catch that pitch!

7
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:38,990
He's beyond a high schooler.

8
00:00:38,990 --> 00:00:42,830
I laughed when I first heard about him,
but actually seeing what he can do...

9
00:00:43,580 --> 00:00:45,710
He doesn't even seem human!

10
00:00:46,170 --> 00:00:49,050
No wonder they call him a Unicorn.

11
00:02:19,010 --> 00:02:23,010
THERE'S A UNICORN UP AHEAD
SATURDAY, MAY 9th

12
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:26,270
Okay, midterms are next week.

13
00:02:26,270 --> 00:02:27,810
- You serious?
- What a pain!

14
00:02:27,810 --> 00:02:30,770
Which means that all club activities 
are suspended for the week.

15
00:02:31,310 --> 00:02:34,360
Make sure to review everything
we've covered so far.

16
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:37,070
So, it's here at last!

17
00:02:37,070 --> 00:02:41,200
Since it's our first test since starting
middle school, I'm kinda nervous!

18
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:43,120
What about you, Ogami?

19
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:44,490
Whoa, scary!

20
00:02:44,490 --> 00:02:45,410
Huh?

21
00:02:45,410 --> 00:02:47,120
You look kinda pissed!

22
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:49,080
No, it's not like that.

23
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:52,380
More like, "A test! All right,
I'm gonna kill it!"

24
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:54,460
I mean, your bloodlust is intense!

25
00:02:54,460 --> 00:02:56,300
He straight up looks
like an assassin, doesn't he?

26
00:02:56,670 --> 00:03:00,800
<i>Boss, don't go blowing your cover
over something this stupid!</i>

27
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:04,430
Uh, this is my first time
dealing with midterms!

28
00:03:04,430 --> 00:03:06,220
What should I do, Master?

29
00:03:06,220 --> 00:03:08,100
I mean, it's everyone's first time.

30
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:10,690
Let's do our best, Noren!

31
00:03:10,690 --> 00:03:11,940
You just suddenly popped up!

32
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:16,030
Ogami, you already study ahead
 and review as you go.

33
00:03:16,030 --> 00:03:18,530
I think you'll be fine
just doing what you normally do.

34
00:03:18,820 --> 00:03:21,780
Thank you for your words
of wisdom, Master!

35
00:03:21,780 --> 00:03:24,080
Seriously, what is with that energy?

36
00:03:25,740 --> 00:03:26,700
Morning!

37
00:03:26,700 --> 00:03:28,040
Oh, hey, Noren!

38
00:03:28,040 --> 00:03:28,870
Morning!

39
00:03:30,290 --> 00:03:31,330
So bright!

40
00:03:31,330 --> 00:03:33,670
You're glowing! What happened to you?

41
00:03:33,670 --> 00:03:35,210
So, here's the thing...

42
00:03:35,210 --> 00:03:38,460
You know how everybody goes into
 study mode during testing week, right?

43
00:03:38,460 --> 00:03:40,880
They have no time
for their thoughts to wander.

44
00:03:41,260 --> 00:03:44,390
Which means nobody's been
 confessing their love to me!

45
00:03:44,390 --> 00:03:45,350
R-Right.

46
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:48,430
I've been sleeping so well
with zero stress!

47
00:03:48,430 --> 00:03:50,890
I wish it could be test week forever!

48
00:03:50,890 --> 00:03:52,900
You've got it rough, too, huh?

49
00:03:52,900 --> 00:03:54,650
I'm actually starting to worry about you.

50
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:56,150
Oh, sorry.

51
00:03:56,860 --> 00:03:57,650
Huh?

52
00:03:59,150 --> 00:04:01,360
Your face is wrecked!
You're all dried out!

53
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:02,570
Oh! Morning!

54
00:04:02,570 --> 00:04:05,120
What's with those eye bags?
Did you not sleep?

55
00:04:05,120 --> 00:04:07,410
Huh? What happened to you, Ogami?

56
00:04:07,410 --> 00:04:09,330
"Glowing" and "dried out"?

57
00:04:09,330 --> 00:04:11,750
What is with this couple?
The contrast is insane!

58
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:13,790
Whoa! Those eye bags are bad!

59
00:04:14,330 --> 00:04:17,340
You really need to get some sleep, Ogami!

60
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:18,500
Yeah.

61
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:20,590
I know that logically, but...

62
00:04:23,300 --> 00:04:24,720
Huh? It's morning already?

63
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:27,850
It's like I just can't stop myself.

64
00:04:27,850 --> 00:04:29,600
How do I express this feeling?

65
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:35,150
It's kind of like how a boxer knows
rest is important before a match...

66
00:04:35,150 --> 00:04:38,360
but still winds up overtraining anyway.

67
00:04:38,650 --> 00:04:40,400
Strange metaphors aside,

68
00:04:40,400 --> 00:04:42,820
you're basically saying that
you're trying way too hard.

69
00:04:50,660 --> 00:04:51,540
Want one?

70
00:04:51,910 --> 00:04:52,960
It helps you relax.

71
00:04:52,960 --> 00:04:53,870
I don't need that!

72
00:04:55,170 --> 00:04:56,830
I'm telling you...

73
00:04:57,170 --> 00:04:58,960
You're overdoing it, Boss.

74
00:04:59,380 --> 00:05:01,300
Pipe down. Mind your own business.

75
00:05:01,630 --> 00:05:03,720
Believe me, I'd love to!

76
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:06,470
Telling someone not to study
too hard is such a nonsense problem!

77
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:11,850
I've got other plans tonight,
so go eat dinner at Mama's place, okay?

78
00:05:11,850 --> 00:05:14,350
Huh? I can eat wherever Iâ€”

79
00:05:14,350 --> 00:05:15,440
Just go, all right?

80
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:17,610
Consider it a change of pace.

81
00:05:17,610 --> 00:05:18,730
RAMEN

82
00:05:18,730 --> 00:05:19,980
You can head out now.

83
00:05:20,360 --> 00:05:21,690
Huh? Already?

84
00:05:21,690 --> 00:05:23,900
It's test week, isn't it?

85
00:05:23,900 --> 00:05:25,280
I'm fine.

86
00:05:25,280 --> 00:05:28,620
I may not look it, but I actually do study
seriously on a regular basis, you know.

87
00:05:28,620 --> 00:05:29,910
Doesn't matter.

88
00:05:29,910 --> 00:05:33,040
At this rate, we're not gonna get
many more customers tonight anyway.

89
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:34,120
Okay.

90
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:34,750
NATSUKIYA

91
00:05:34,750 --> 00:05:37,130
Then I'm heading out!

92
00:05:40,670 --> 00:05:42,340
Ogami?

93
00:05:47,890 --> 00:05:49,430
Where's he going?

94
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:53,350
Wait, whoa!

95
00:05:53,350 --> 00:05:56,390
He's heading deeper and deeper
into a really sketchy area!

96
00:05:56,390 --> 00:05:58,810
Oh, Juzo!

97
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:00,690
Good evening!

98
00:06:00,690 --> 00:06:01,320
BAR JABAMI

99
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:03,940
Hey. Gekota, was it?

100
00:06:03,940 --> 00:06:06,030
Long time no see, little fish!

101
00:06:06,780 --> 00:06:07,860
You open?

102
00:06:07,860 --> 00:06:11,700
Open for freakin' business, babe!

103
00:06:11,700 --> 00:06:14,330
I came by to score some dinner...

104
00:06:14,330 --> 00:06:14,950
BAR JABAMI

105
00:06:14,950 --> 00:06:17,960
...but is Kyosuke, I mean Mama, here?

106
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:19,250
Abso-freakin'-lutely!

107
00:06:19,630 --> 00:06:20,960
Mama Nagisa!

108
00:06:20,960 --> 00:06:24,460
Your itty-bitty boyfriend's here!

109
00:06:25,840 --> 00:06:28,010
Wh-What kind of setup is this?

110
00:06:30,300 --> 00:06:33,260
Ah, no matter how many times I see you,
you're still just too adorable!

111
00:06:33,260 --> 00:06:34,390
I could eat you right up!

112
00:06:34,810 --> 00:06:37,850
Your pilaf's always good, Mama.

113
00:06:38,310 --> 00:06:40,940
My, my... Geko, could I get
an oolong tea for him?

114
00:06:40,940 --> 00:06:42,230
Coming right up!

115
00:06:44,610 --> 00:06:48,700
I didn't want anyone suspecting
 that I had a secret child,

116
00:06:48,700 --> 00:06:50,620
so I told everyone that you're my nephew.

117
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:51,660
I see.

118
00:06:51,660 --> 00:06:55,580
Honestly, when you first turned young,
I was stunned.

119
00:06:56,950 --> 00:06:59,290
Oh, Neko, welcome!

120
00:06:59,870 --> 00:07:03,380
Oh my, what's this?
Who's this delicious-looking little cutie?

121
00:07:06,130 --> 00:07:07,590
He's actually Boss.

122
00:07:07,590 --> 00:07:08,510
Huh?

123
00:07:09,180 --> 00:07:13,260
I know I can trust you, and when things
go sideways, you always come through.

124
00:07:13,260 --> 00:07:14,390
So, this really helps.

125
00:07:14,390 --> 00:07:17,060
Leave it to me, little Juzo.

126
00:07:17,060 --> 00:07:19,730
Honestly, now I wanna protect you
even more than before.

127
00:07:20,100 --> 00:07:21,560
I'm beat!

128
00:07:22,020 --> 00:07:23,770
Mama, listen to this.

129
00:07:23,770 --> 00:07:25,980
The new guy screwed up royally today.

130
00:07:26,440 --> 00:07:27,320
Eri?

131
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:28,650
What are you doing here?

132
00:07:28,650 --> 00:07:30,360
Eri, welcome back!

133
00:07:30,360 --> 00:07:31,780
The usual for you?

134
00:07:31,780 --> 00:07:33,160
Yeah, please!

135
00:07:33,570 --> 00:07:36,080
I tell you, kids these days...

136
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:37,330
- Oh, stop!
- Jeez!

137
00:07:37,330 --> 00:07:39,660
- I told him to mind his own business.
- That guy should mind his business.

138
00:07:42,290 --> 00:07:44,500
I was wondering how you got
those bags under your eyes.

139
00:07:44,500 --> 00:07:45,710
So, that's what's going on?

140
00:07:45,710 --> 00:07:47,000
Oh, shut up.

141
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,260
Never mind that. Is it okay for you
to be drinking in a place like this?

142
00:07:49,260 --> 00:07:50,300
What about Kozue?

143
00:07:50,300 --> 00:07:52,180
It's fine, it's fine!

144
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:56,560
She doesn't mind me stopping in
for one drink on the way home...

145
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:57,810
every once in a while.

146
00:07:58,270 --> 00:08:00,520
That girl's got a good head
on her shoulders.

147
00:08:03,020 --> 00:08:04,270
I see.

148
00:08:04,270 --> 00:08:05,520
Yeah, I guess she does.

149
00:08:09,110 --> 00:08:10,780
So, pulling all-nighters to study...

150
00:08:10,780 --> 00:08:12,070
Why not?

151
00:08:12,070 --> 00:08:15,030
Go into that test as you are
and bomb it as you are.

152
00:08:15,030 --> 00:08:15,910
Hey, come on!

153
00:08:15,910 --> 00:08:19,330
I'm not asking you to comfort me
or anything, but that's brutal!

154
00:08:19,330 --> 00:08:21,790
No, that's not what I meant.

155
00:08:21,790 --> 00:08:22,420
Huh?

156
00:08:24,920 --> 00:08:29,920
Before you ended up in that body,
when you were still out there working...

157
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:32,220
the mission was everything.

158
00:08:33,970 --> 00:08:36,260
You were never allowed to fail, right?

159
00:08:36,260 --> 00:08:39,100
Even back when you used to drink here,
part of you was always wound tight.

160
00:08:39,100 --> 00:08:42,440
But I don't think you need
that kind of mindset for studying.

161
00:08:42,810 --> 00:08:45,770
Now that you're a middle schooler,
it's okay to screw up sometimes.

162
00:08:46,110 --> 00:08:49,030
You might as well take advantage of it
and make all the mistakes...

163
00:08:49,030 --> 00:08:51,990
you never got to make before.
And not just with studying, either.

164
00:08:53,150 --> 00:08:55,990
Besides, setting aside
 sleep deprivation for the moment...

165
00:08:56,490 --> 00:08:59,200
ever since you started middle school...

166
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:01,200
you've been looking
a whole lot more alive.

167
00:09:03,710 --> 00:09:04,500
BAR JABAMI

168
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:05,630
See ya, Mama.

169
00:09:05,630 --> 00:09:06,250
BAR JABAMI

170
00:09:06,250 --> 00:09:07,250
Thanks for the drink!

171
00:09:07,250 --> 00:09:09,170
Okay, see you next time!

172
00:09:09,170 --> 00:09:12,760
And you, quit standing there spacing out
and walk her to the station!

173
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:14,050
R-Right.

174
00:09:17,930 --> 00:09:19,260
What?

175
00:09:19,260 --> 00:09:24,020
He went into that crossdresser bar and 
came back out with a hot older lady!

176
00:09:24,020 --> 00:09:26,480
Just who is Ogami?

177
00:09:26,480 --> 00:09:27,900
MIDTERM EXAMS (DAY 1)
SOCIAL STUDIES - MATH - SCIENCE

178
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:31,980
In the end, I wouldn't say
I bombed the test...

179
00:09:31,980 --> 00:09:35,490
but I made a few careless mistakes,
forgot a few things and did about average.

180
00:09:35,490 --> 00:09:36,360
MATH MIDTERM EXAM
YEAR: 1, CLASS: E, NAME: JUZO OGAMI

181
00:09:36,360 --> 00:09:37,660
Well, for this time...

182
00:09:38,070 --> 00:09:39,950
I guess this is about
what I should've expected.

183
00:09:39,950 --> 00:09:43,000
I'll learn from it and 
do better on finals.

184
00:09:52,880 --> 00:09:53,970
Come to think of it...

185
00:09:54,470 --> 00:09:56,970
Well, I'm just here for the ramen, so...

186
00:09:57,260 --> 00:10:00,390
Maybe Ogami really isn't normal.

187
00:10:00,970 --> 00:10:02,890
So, keep your hands off my girl.

188
00:10:02,890 --> 00:10:04,810
- It's more than just him being weird.
- Now get lost.

189
00:10:04,810 --> 00:10:05,600
What is it?

190
00:10:06,520 --> 00:10:08,690
He feels more like
somebody's uncle or a dad...

191
00:10:08,690 --> 00:10:11,020
like he's from
a totally different age group.

192
00:10:11,770 --> 00:10:14,490
Is he really a middle school student?

193
00:10:19,030 --> 00:10:19,990
HOME EC ROOM

194
00:10:19,990 --> 00:10:21,280
Hold it down like this...

195
00:10:21,830 --> 00:10:26,870
pass the thread between the button
and the fabric three or four times.

196
00:10:27,420 --> 00:10:31,090
Don't forget to stick your thumb in here
to leave a little slack.

197
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:34,300
Then wrap the thread
around that slack over and over,

198
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:35,800
and that gives you the thread shank.

199
00:10:36,090 --> 00:10:37,680
Make a loop.

200
00:10:37,680 --> 00:10:38,300
Pull tight.

201
00:10:38,630 --> 00:10:40,470
And to finish it off, tie a knot.

202
00:10:42,100 --> 00:10:43,760
And there, done.

203
00:10:44,220 --> 00:10:46,180
See? Easy, right?

204
00:10:46,180 --> 00:10:48,980
Oh! So, that's how you sew on a button!

205
00:10:48,980 --> 00:10:51,230
Once you get used to it,
it doesn't even take ten minutes.

206
00:10:51,560 --> 00:10:54,030
And honestly, even just repairing
a button yourself...

207
00:10:54,030 --> 00:10:56,490
might make you feel
more attached to your clothes.

208
00:10:56,490 --> 00:10:57,450
I see!

209
00:10:57,900 --> 00:10:59,200
It's like cars and motorcycles.

210
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:01,570
The more you work on them yourself,
the more attached you get.

211
00:11:01,570 --> 00:11:04,950
That is a weirdly un-middle-schooler-like
way to relate to what I just said.

212
00:11:05,790 --> 00:11:07,200
Anyway, why don't you give it a try?

213
00:11:07,790 --> 00:11:09,710
If you get stuck, just ask for help.

214
00:11:09,710 --> 00:11:10,620
'Kay!

215
00:11:11,040 --> 00:11:13,000
So, that's what needles can be used for!

216
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:13,630
Huh?

217
00:11:14,420 --> 00:11:17,920
I always thought they were meant
to be coated in poison to stab people.

218
00:11:17,920 --> 00:11:20,130
That's... not wrong, but...

219
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:24,010
Huh?

220
00:11:24,010 --> 00:11:26,350
The club president made it look easy.

221
00:11:27,140 --> 00:11:28,140
What is that?

222
00:11:28,140 --> 00:11:29,640
How did you mess it up like that?

223
00:11:29,640 --> 00:11:30,270
Noren?

224
00:11:31,480 --> 00:11:32,480
Me, too!

225
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:33,400
Hey...

226
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:36,980
Doing this has reminded me
 how terrible I am at sewing!

227
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:39,700
Well, that's what this club, right?

228
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:41,740
I'm gonna go ask the senpais for help!

229
00:11:41,740 --> 00:11:42,910
Me, too!

230
00:11:56,210 --> 00:11:57,130
That's...

231
00:11:57,590 --> 00:11:58,760
Kito-senpai!

232
00:11:58,760 --> 00:12:00,130
Are you not heading home yet?

233
00:12:00,590 --> 00:12:03,050
Oh, hey, you two!

234
00:12:03,050 --> 00:12:05,430
I forgot to water these guys.

235
00:12:05,970 --> 00:12:07,680
Sunflowers?

236
00:12:07,680 --> 00:12:09,640
Yep. I planted the seeds early...

237
00:12:10,100 --> 00:12:12,850
so they should probably bloom
before summer vacation.

238
00:12:13,690 --> 00:12:14,900
I can't wait!

239
00:12:17,860 --> 00:12:19,240
Did something happen?

240
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:20,320
Hm?

241
00:12:20,320 --> 00:12:23,570
I mean, you seem
to be in a good mood.

242
00:12:25,070 --> 00:12:26,870
It's not so much that something happened.

243
00:12:26,870 --> 00:12:29,160
It's more like I really like
the home ec club.

244
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:29,870
Yeah.

245
00:12:30,370 --> 00:12:32,870
Kito loves plants.

246
00:12:33,370 --> 00:12:35,710
President Shiraishi's into cooking
in general.

247
00:12:36,250 --> 00:12:38,170
Yamaoka likes baking sweet treats.

248
00:12:38,630 --> 00:12:42,170
And Tamada and Nishimura
are really good at handicrafts!

249
00:12:42,800 --> 00:12:45,430
We all do different things
together as a club,

250
00:12:45,430 --> 00:12:49,640
but every one of them has their own
little world that they genuinely love!

251
00:12:50,020 --> 00:12:52,560
So, nobody's just hanging around
to gossip or pry,

252
00:12:52,560 --> 00:12:54,060
and they're all really easy to talk to!

253
00:12:54,690 --> 00:12:57,610
I'm really glad I joined the home ec club!

254
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:01,990
Um, today's club activity is...

255
00:13:01,990 --> 00:13:04,490
making rice balls for the baseball team.

256
00:13:05,450 --> 00:13:06,950
They need a lot, so it'll be tough...

257
00:13:07,410 --> 00:13:10,040
but they'll really appreciate it,
so let's do our best!

258
00:13:10,740 --> 00:13:12,290
Is something wrong?

259
00:13:12,290 --> 00:13:14,170
Well, the thing is...

260
00:13:14,710 --> 00:13:17,380
our team isn't the only one 
that uses the practice field.

261
00:13:17,380 --> 00:13:19,710
There's a senior league team 
that rents it as well.

262
00:13:20,210 --> 00:13:23,170
Today's delivery is actually for them...

263
00:13:23,550 --> 00:13:25,180
and a Unicorn is on that team.

264
00:13:27,090 --> 00:13:29,600
Yeah, that's the problem.

265
00:13:30,140 --> 00:13:34,060
Just because he's a Unicorn doesn't
automatically mean he's after you, Noren.

266
00:13:34,060 --> 00:13:38,310
That's just a rumor after all,
and it's possible nothing'll happen.

267
00:13:38,810 --> 00:13:40,940
Still, if you two
aren't comfortable with it,

268
00:13:40,940 --> 00:13:43,320
you don't need to be
 there for the delivery.

269
00:13:43,820 --> 00:13:44,950
It's up to you.

270
00:13:46,490 --> 00:13:47,990
I get how you feel.

271
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:50,450
You can decide.

272
00:13:53,450 --> 00:13:54,500
Move up, move up closer!

273
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:55,250
One more!

274
00:13:55,250 --> 00:13:56,710
- Let me hear you!
- Ready!

275
00:13:57,540 --> 00:13:59,630
Hey, we brought some snacks for you guys!

276
00:13:59,630 --> 00:14:01,670
Oh, thanks!

277
00:14:01,670 --> 00:14:02,800
Everybody, gather up!

278
00:14:03,630 --> 00:14:04,510
Thanks!

279
00:14:04,510 --> 00:14:05,260
No problem!

280
00:14:06,260 --> 00:14:07,430
Looks great!

281
00:14:07,430 --> 00:14:08,390
Time to eat!

282
00:14:08,390 --> 00:14:09,470
Hey, hurry up!

283
00:14:10,550 --> 00:14:12,060
Oh, they're here?

284
00:14:12,510 --> 00:14:13,810
Oh, that tall guy.

285
00:14:13,810 --> 00:14:15,680
He's the one
they were talking about.

286
00:14:19,190 --> 00:14:20,400
I see.

287
00:14:20,400 --> 00:14:23,320
You can tell right away
from the look of him.

288
00:14:27,610 --> 00:14:28,990
Tenma Tendo.

289
00:14:28,990 --> 00:14:30,320
He's huge!

290
00:14:30,320 --> 00:14:31,910
Is he really a middle schooler?

291
00:14:31,910 --> 00:14:33,740
He's gotta be pushing 190 cm!

292
00:14:33,740 --> 00:14:35,410
Oh, rice balls!

293
00:14:35,410 --> 00:14:36,580
Thanks a ton!

294
00:14:36,580 --> 00:14:38,250
Sorry I took so long getting over here!

295
00:14:38,670 --> 00:14:39,710
Down the hatch!

296
00:14:42,460 --> 00:14:45,260
Man, that's good! Total energy boost!

297
00:14:47,220 --> 00:14:48,840
Oh, right.

298
00:14:48,840 --> 00:14:51,760
You two are here, huh?
I was hoping to talk to you for a sec!

299
00:14:52,350 --> 00:14:54,680
You're Noren and Juzo, right?

300
00:14:54,680 --> 00:14:56,390
You've been getting
a lot of attention lately.

301
00:14:57,310 --> 00:14:58,270
He's a giant!

302
00:14:58,890 --> 00:15:01,980
All right, let's see
whether the rumors are true.

303
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:05,190
I don't expect him to come
right out with it immediately, but...

304
00:15:05,190 --> 00:15:06,490
Let's duel.

305
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:10,490
If I win, I get to be
Noren's boyfriend, right?

306
00:15:10,860 --> 00:15:11,660
Wha...

307
00:15:12,030 --> 00:15:15,120
Oh, come on. So, the rumors are true
and you're opening with that?

308
00:15:15,580 --> 00:15:16,870
Oh, no!

309
00:15:17,250 --> 00:15:18,460
Hey, Tenma!

310
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:22,210
No, no! We're just chatting
while I refuel. That's all!

311
00:15:22,580 --> 00:15:24,340
Don't just spring
stuff like that on me!

312
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:26,880
We don't even know each other!
It's not happening!

313
00:15:26,880 --> 00:15:27,720
Right?

314
00:15:28,300 --> 00:15:30,970
It's not like I'm into you or anything.

315
00:15:30,970 --> 00:15:31,800
Sorry.

316
00:15:32,140 --> 00:15:32,930
Huh?

317
00:15:33,390 --> 00:15:36,430
It's not challenging you 
because I wanna go out with her.

318
00:15:36,720 --> 00:15:41,020
It's more that I wanna crush you
 because you're in my way.

319
00:15:41,020 --> 00:15:41,900
What?

320
00:15:42,900 --> 00:15:47,360
I think the thing that inspires people
most in this world is sports!

321
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:49,530
That's why everyone should be watching me!

322
00:15:49,530 --> 00:15:52,070
No, everyone needs to watch me!

323
00:15:52,070 --> 00:15:53,200
Because I'm gonna become...

324
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:58,040
the first true triple threat sportsman
in human history, a superman!

325
00:15:58,500 --> 00:16:00,120
Triple threat?

326
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:02,710
You mean like being
both a pitcher and a batter?

327
00:16:02,710 --> 00:16:03,460
Boss!

328
00:16:03,460 --> 00:16:06,050
I looked it up,
and that is not what he means!

329
00:16:06,050 --> 00:16:06,750
Huh?

330
00:16:06,750 --> 00:16:09,380
Not a triple threat baseball player!

331
00:16:09,380 --> 00:16:11,430
A triple threat sportsman!

332
00:16:11,430 --> 00:16:12,380
In other words...

333
00:16:12,380 --> 00:16:13,090
ACE TENDO LEADS TEAM TO JP CHAMPIONSHIP 
JP YOUTH ACE STRIKER TENDO SCORES HAT TRICK

334
00:16:13,090 --> 00:16:14,260
Senior league baseball!

335
00:16:14,260 --> 00:16:14,890
CHAMPION PITCHER
TENMA TENDO

336
00:16:15,260 --> 00:16:16,180
Ace striker in soccer!

337
00:16:16,180 --> 00:16:16,810
MIDDLE SCHOOL PRODIGY STRIKER
TENMA TENDO

338
00:16:16,810 --> 00:16:17,970
Middle school basketball!

339
00:16:17,970 --> 00:16:18,680
TENMA TENDO
SUPERSTAR OF THE BASKETBALL WORLD

340
00:16:18,680 --> 00:16:22,230
He's the ace in all three, and he keeps
racking up national titles, too!

341
00:16:22,230 --> 00:16:22,850
ULTIMATE MIDDLE SCHOOLER
TENMA TENDO

342
00:16:23,650 --> 00:16:27,360
A Unicorn, the man
with the ultimate physical gift!

343
00:16:28,110 --> 00:16:31,360
The MLB, the NBA, the Premier League.

344
00:16:31,650 --> 00:16:34,870
I'm gonna become
the best player in all of them!

345
00:16:35,370 --> 00:16:36,330
What?

346
00:16:36,330 --> 00:16:37,910
Is that even possible?

347
00:16:37,910 --> 00:16:39,200
I have no idea.

348
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:42,290
I've heard of some pros
who can do two sports, but...

349
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,290
I get it now.

350
00:16:44,290 --> 00:16:47,040
So, basically, you're a sports freak
who loves the spotlight...

351
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:50,300
and can't stand anybody
getting more attention than you.

352
00:16:50,300 --> 00:16:52,930
Huh? Can't stand? Not really.

353
00:16:53,800 --> 00:16:56,470
You're just some background extra
from the home ec club, right?

354
00:16:56,470 --> 00:16:57,350
To begin with...

355
00:16:57,680 --> 00:17:00,350
I'm not that interested in people
from some little play club

356
00:17:00,350 --> 00:17:01,890
whose existence doesn't even matter.

357
00:17:03,060 --> 00:17:03,890
However...

358
00:17:04,190 --> 00:17:05,900
you are annoying.

359
00:17:06,310 --> 00:17:08,690
Hey! What the hell
kind of rude crap is that?

360
00:17:08,690 --> 00:17:11,190
Ah, no, I mean,
I'm happy about the rice balls!

361
00:17:11,190 --> 00:17:12,400
It saves me from having to buy food!

362
00:17:12,400 --> 00:17:14,860
- You need to stop talking! Like, now!
- Huh?

363
00:17:14,860 --> 00:17:15,700
It's fine.

364
00:17:16,120 --> 00:17:18,160
Then let's do it. A duel.

365
00:17:18,660 --> 00:17:19,830
Ogami!

366
00:17:19,830 --> 00:17:22,000
He doesn't even sound
like he's dead set on it!

367
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:24,370
Nope. I'm the one who's pissed off now.

368
00:17:24,710 --> 00:17:29,380
This guy didn't just insult me.
He casually dissed the ladies, too.

369
00:17:29,670 --> 00:17:32,510
Do your superman hotshot
or triple threat stuff if you want.

370
00:17:32,880 --> 00:17:35,550
But don't look down on home ec, asshole!

371
00:17:37,430 --> 00:17:38,680
All right, it's settled!

372
00:17:39,470 --> 00:17:41,220
What should we compete in?

373
00:17:41,560 --> 00:17:43,270
Okay, let's make it futsal!

374
00:17:43,600 --> 00:17:45,600
One week from now, in the gym.

375
00:17:45,940 --> 00:17:49,190
I'll bring one other person, but you guys
can bring as many as you want.

376
00:17:49,650 --> 00:17:52,070
Huh? Since when do I need a handicap?

377
00:17:52,070 --> 00:17:54,070
No, take the handicap!

378
00:17:55,610 --> 00:17:59,450
Suit yourself, but without one,
this won't even be a match.

379
00:17:59,450 --> 00:18:01,580
Anyway, do what you want.

380
00:18:02,040 --> 00:18:04,500
I'm so sorry, home ec club!

381
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:06,870
Please let me apologize on his behalf.

382
00:18:06,870 --> 00:18:08,330
Uh, right, okay.

383
00:18:08,630 --> 00:18:11,170
And you all still treat him
like he's special?

384
00:18:11,170 --> 00:18:14,090
Yeah. Normally, if you split your time
between three different sports,

385
00:18:14,090 --> 00:18:16,050
you only have a limited time
for each one, right?

386
00:18:16,590 --> 00:18:21,510
But he overwhelms that limitation
through sheer dominance.

387
00:18:22,100 --> 00:18:24,560
We apologize for his rudeness, too.

388
00:18:24,890 --> 00:18:27,600
But if I may say one thing...

389
00:18:28,190 --> 00:18:30,270
as a teammate...

390
00:18:30,270 --> 00:18:32,400
he's the greatest hero!

391
00:18:32,400 --> 00:18:34,360
But as an opponent...

392
00:18:34,860 --> 00:18:36,860
he's the strongest villain!

393
00:18:38,740 --> 00:18:39,360
HOME EC ROOM

394
00:18:39,360 --> 00:18:40,950
Forget the details.

395
00:18:41,700 --> 00:18:45,950
He looked down on my club members, so
you go out there and wreck his ass, Ogami!

396
00:18:46,290 --> 00:18:48,460
Leave it to me, boss!

397
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:51,040
I'll make him regret the day he was born!

398
00:18:51,040 --> 00:18:53,340
<i>This is civilian conversation, right?</i>

399
00:18:53,920 --> 00:18:55,630
But it's futsal, right?

400
00:18:55,630 --> 00:18:57,800
Besides Ogami, who else would even...

401
00:18:57,800 --> 00:18:59,130
Huh? Noren?

402
00:19:00,390 --> 00:19:01,890
Don't just spring
something like that on me!

403
00:19:02,220 --> 00:19:04,890
We don't even know each other!
It's not happening!

404
00:19:04,890 --> 00:19:05,890
Right?

405
00:19:06,350 --> 00:19:08,980
It's not like I'm into you or anything.

406
00:19:08,980 --> 00:19:10,400
Sorry.

407
00:19:10,730 --> 00:19:12,940
This is so humiliating!

408
00:19:12,940 --> 00:19:14,730
I mean, sure,
there was context leading up to it,

409
00:19:14,730 --> 00:19:17,150
but in the end, it totally came off like,
"Stop fighting over me!"

410
00:19:17,150 --> 00:19:20,950
And then, "It's not like I'm into you,"
like I'm some cringey self-important girl!

411
00:19:20,950 --> 00:19:23,660
No, no, overthinking it like that
is way too self-absorbed...

412
00:19:23,990 --> 00:19:26,040
- ...and I won't think about it anymoreâ€”
- I'll do it.

413
00:19:26,950 --> 00:19:28,120
Shin?

414
00:19:28,120 --> 00:19:29,670
You're still here?

415
00:19:29,670 --> 00:19:32,290
That guy made my beloved Noren say...

416
00:19:32,670 --> 00:19:34,340
"Stop fighting over me!"

417
00:19:34,340 --> 00:19:38,300
"Uh, I'm not into you," like she was
some cringey self-important girl!

418
00:19:38,300 --> 00:19:39,300
That's unforgivable!

419
00:19:39,300 --> 00:19:40,680
No!

420
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:42,340
Please don't bring it up again!

421
00:19:42,340 --> 00:19:43,180
Uh...

422
00:19:43,470 --> 00:19:46,220
if it doesn't have to be
exactly two-on-two, I could join, too.

423
00:19:46,640 --> 00:19:49,640
The home ec club
isn't just messing around,

424
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:51,980
and we all take
what we care about seriously.

425
00:19:51,980 --> 00:19:53,270
Kito...

426
00:19:53,690 --> 00:19:55,650
And besides, he made Mitsuoka say...

427
00:19:56,280 --> 00:19:58,150
"Stop fighting over me!"

428
00:19:58,150 --> 00:20:01,530
"Uh, I'm not into you," like she was
some cringey self-important girl!

429
00:20:01,530 --> 00:20:03,570
Please stop repeating that already!

430
00:20:05,240 --> 00:20:06,660
And anyway...

431
00:20:06,660 --> 00:20:10,000
I don't even care about the whole
"dating as the prize in a duel" thing.

432
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:11,420
More than anything...

433
00:20:11,420 --> 00:20:15,380
what I can't forgive is him mocking
the home ec club I love so much!

434
00:20:15,380 --> 00:20:16,340
So...

435
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:18,420
You'd better win.

436
00:20:18,420 --> 00:20:19,510
Okay?

437
00:20:20,010 --> 00:20:20,920
You got it!

438
00:21:55,390 --> 00:21:59,230
Jeez, asking me out of nowhere to help
with some duel? What the hell is that?

439
00:21:59,900 --> 00:22:03,570
And Mitsuoka... That's the rich girl
at your school, right?

440
00:22:03,570 --> 00:22:04,400
Why her?

441
00:22:04,900 --> 00:22:06,700
Well, no real reason.

442
00:22:06,700 --> 00:22:07,860
Hey!

443
00:22:09,490 --> 00:22:11,370
This is weird.

444
00:22:11,370 --> 00:22:13,750
You've never gone out of your way
to pick a fight before.

445
00:22:14,370 --> 00:22:17,500
Well, that's because they came to me
first, so it just happened.

446
00:22:17,500 --> 00:22:19,250
Even so!

447
00:22:19,250 --> 00:22:22,050
If you really didn't care at all,
you'd have just ignored them.

448
00:22:22,050 --> 00:22:23,550
Yeah, true.

449
00:22:23,550 --> 00:22:24,720
What is it, though?

450
00:22:29,550 --> 00:22:31,350
When I look at that Ogami guy...

451
00:22:31,970 --> 00:22:34,350
I get all restless. 
There's something about him.

452
00:22:37,440 --> 00:22:40,520
Anyway, I'm only doing
the bare minimum out there.

453
00:22:40,520 --> 00:22:42,020
Yeah, okay!

454
00:22:42,270 --> 00:22:44,440
I wasn't expecting much from you
to begin with.

455
00:22:45,690 --> 00:22:47,400
You always have to add...

456
00:22:47,400 --> 00:22:49,360
one extra smart-ass comment!

457
00:22:49,950 --> 00:22:52,120
Crap! I put too much into that
without thinking!

458
00:22:54,910 --> 00:22:55,910
Whoa!

459
00:22:56,250 --> 00:22:59,580
He completely killed that momentum!
He really is nothing short of a prodigy!

460
00:23:00,170 --> 00:23:01,130
Nice pass!

461
00:23:01,130 --> 00:23:03,300
Man, you're irritating!

462
00:23:04,380 --> 00:23:05,590
Another Mitsuoka duel!

463
00:23:05,590 --> 00:23:07,050
And this time, it's against a Unicorn!

464
00:23:07,050 --> 00:23:08,300
Three-on-two futsal!

465
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:10,970
Is this even gonna be a real match?

466
00:23:11,760 --> 00:23:12,720
Listen up.

467
00:23:12,720 --> 00:23:16,100
If you win, then we go
by the usual Mitsuoka duel rules.

468
00:23:16,430 --> 00:23:19,230
But if we win, there's one condition.

469
00:23:19,690 --> 00:23:20,690
What?

470
00:23:21,020 --> 00:23:23,230
You mocked the Home Ec Club.

471
00:23:23,230 --> 00:23:24,940
So, apologize to the ladies.

472
00:23:25,570 --> 00:23:27,360
Huh? Sure, fine.

473
00:23:27,690 --> 00:23:28,860
But are you sure?

474
00:23:28,860 --> 00:23:31,820
That's basically the same thing
as saying, "Don't apologize," you know.

475
00:23:31,820 --> 00:23:33,780
Because I'm absolutely going to win.

476
00:23:34,200 --> 00:23:34,910
What?

